# winlew.co/xl1/ — served from this host, no redirect.
#
# This file used to send everything under /xl1/ to a Netlify copy, because the
# node data changed every five minutes and an uploaded copy could never keep up.
#
# It does not need to any more. The producer data now lives in a small public
# repository the nodes write directly:
#
#   https://github.com/LewSales/xl1-status-data
#
# and the pages fetch it cross-origin from raw.githubusercontent, which sends
# access-control-allow-origin: *. So the only thing that has to be uploaded here
# is the pages themselves, and those change rarely.
#
# That is strictly better than the redirect was: the address bar stays on
# winlew.co instead of bouncing to a netlify.app domain, and there is no build
# step between a node publishing and a visitor seeing it.
#
# Why the redirect went away rather than being tidied: routing every data update
# through a site deploy cost about 550 deploys a day, exhausted the host's
# monthly build allowance in three days, and froze the pages on an hour-old
# snapshot while both producers were healthy. Publishing a JSON file should not
# rebuild a website.

# Never allow Apache to turn a missing index into a public file inventory.
# Individual, explicitly named data files remain directly fetchable.
Options -Indexes

# The pages are small and change rarely, but when one does change a visitor
# holding a cached copy would keep polling with the old data URL. Revalidate.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.html$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>

# The shared/*.test.js files are Node tests kept beside the code they test.
# They are not part of any page, so do not serve them.
<FilesMatch "\.test\.js$">
  <IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
  </IfModule>
  <IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order allow,deny
    Deny from all
  </IfModule>
</FilesMatch>
